ot diluting shareholders","ok":true,"evidence":"Diluted share count -2.1% YoY"},{"label":"Analyst estimates moving higher","ok":null,"evidence":"Estimate-revision feed not connected (Phase 2)"},{"label":"Management guidance increasing","ok":null,"evidence":"Earnings Intelligence Engine not built (Phase 2)"}],"thesis":"Intuit (INTU) screens at opportunity 68.0 with an expectations gap of 30.0. Reality 55.0 reflects +13.9% TTM revenue growth, +27.4% operating margin and +20.0% ROIC; pricing 25.0 reflects a depressed multiple and weak price momentum. Primary theme exposure: AI Software & Agents (trend 72.0). Macro fit for Technology in a Goldilocks regime is 53.0/100.","market_expectation":{"summary":"Priced for stagnation or deterioration; the market is not paying for improvement.","evidence":["EV/Sales 3.6x (0.0th pct of own 5y range)","P/E 16x (0.0th pct of own history)","FCF yield 11.7%","PEG 0.8","12m return -60%, -60% from 52w high"]},"what_market_misses":["Reality (55.0) is running ahead of what is priced (25.0): an expectations gap of +30 pts.","Operating leverage is showing up in margins faster than in the valuation.","Its main theme (AI Software & Agents) has trend 72.0 vs pricing 53.0: the theme itself is under-owned.","Capital is rotating into Technology (+66) but this stock has not yet participated."],"catalysts":["Next quarterly report (roughly 90 days after the last filing on 2026-09-09)","AI Software & Agents: evidence that 'Trust, integration into workflows, proprietary data' is easing via Platforms owning the system of record and the data","Continued rotation into Technology"],"risks":["No engine-flagged risks; standard execution and macro risk apply."],"thesis_break_conditions":["TTM revenue growth falls below 9% (currently 13.9%)","ROIC falls below 15% (currently 20.0%)","Operating margin compresses more than 200 bps YoY (currently 27.4%)","Technology rotation score turns below -20 for two consecutive runs (currently +66)","Adverse regime (Stagflation + Contraction) probability exceeds 55%","Price closes >10% below its 200-day average with negative relative strength","AI Software & Agents theme trend drops below 45"],"break_rules":[{"id":"revenue_growth","label":"TTM revenue growth","metric":"revenue_growth","op":"<","threshold":0.089,"current":0.139},{"id":"roic","label":"ROIC","metric":"roic","op":"<","threshold":0.1497,"current":0.1995},{"id":"margin","label":"Operating margin change YoY","metric":"operating_margin_change","op":"<","threshold":-0.02,"current":0.012907313884065574},{"id":"rotation","label":"Technology rotation score","metric":"sector_rotation","op":"<","threshold":-20,"consecutive":2,"current":66.0},{"id":"regime","label":"P(Stagflation)+P(Contraction)","metric":"adverse_regime_prob","op":">","threshold":55,"current":48.9},{"id":"trend","label":"Distance from 200dma","metric":"dist_200dma","op":"<","threshold":-10,"and_negative_rs":true,"current":-31.6},{"id":"theme","label":"AI Software & Agents theme trend","metric":"theme_trend","theme_id":"ai-software-agents","op":"<","threshold":45,"current":72.0}],"narrative_note":"Narrative from the last 7 morning briefs' theme signals (exposure-weighted).","llm_enriched":true,"theme_exposures":[{"theme_id":"ai-software-agents","theme":"AI Software & Agents","weight":0.3,"order":1,"effective":0.3}],"llm":{"thesis":"Intuit's operating business is still compounding \u2014 TTM revenue +13.9%, operating margin 27.4% (+129bps YoY), FCF +41.5% to $8.66B, ROIC 20%, net debt/EBITDA 0.5x \u2014 yet the equity has de-rated to the 0th percentile of its own five-year range on every multiple (16x P/E vs 75x median, 8.5x P/FCF vs 38.9x, 3.6x EV/Sales vs 12.2x) after a -60% twelve-month drawdown. A 4-5x multiple compression against intact fundamentals is not a growth-deceleration story (growth only slipped from 15.1% to 13.9%); it is the market re-underwriting terminal value, most plausibly on the view that agentic AI disintermediates DIY tax prep and SMB bookkeeping \u2014 the exact fear embedded in the AI Software & Agents theme note about who owns the system of record. The investable question is narrow: does Intuit's proprietary transaction/tax data and distribution let it rent out agents, or does it become the thing agents replace? At 11.7% FCF yield and a 9.1% shareholder yield (7.3% buyback, 1.8% dividend) with a nearly unlevered balance sheet, the price already funds a large part of the bear case, but the tape (-22.5% in one month, -31.6% below the 200-day, MACD negative) says the de-rating is still in progress and the engine's own technical break condition is already violated.","fundamental_read":"Growth is healthy but decelerating at the margin (+13.9% TTM vs +15.1% prior), while margin and cash generation are inflecting up: operating margin 27.4% (+129bps), FCF margin 40.4%, FCF conversion 1.9x net income, ROIC ~20% and ROE 24%. Balance sheet is a non-issue \u2014 $4.7B cash, $2.96B net debt, 0.49x EBITDA, 23x interest coverage \u2014 and the company returned $5.4B of buybacks plus $1.3B dividends while shrinking diluted shares 2.1%. Two quality caveats: SBC is 9.6% of revenue ($2.06B), so headline FCF flatters true owner earnings by roughly a fifth, and 1.9x FCF/net income conversion is unlikely to be a durable run-rate absent working-capital or deferred-revenue tailwinds.","technical_read":"Every trend filter is broken: price $277 sits below the 20- (323), 50- (325) and 200-day (405) averages, -31.6% from the 200-day and -60.3% from the 52-week high, with MACD histogram -6.07. RSI 29.9 is oversold and the 3-month return is still +8.6%, so a reflex bounce is plausible, but oversold in a structural de-rating is not a bottom signal. Reclaiming and holding the 50-day (~325) with positive relative strength would be the first genuine evidence the tape has stopped discounting impairment.","market_expectation":"At 16x earnings, 8.5x FCF and 3.6x EV/Sales \u2014 the cheapest levels of the last five years by a wide margin, against medians of 75x/38.9x/12.2x \u2014 the market is pricing not stagnation but decay: a business whose consumer tax franchise and SMB software annuity are structurally at risk from AI agents and free/direct filing alternatives, with margins and pricing power assumed to mean-revert downward. A PEG of 0.8 implies zero credit for the growth currently being reported. Meanwhile capital is rotating into Technology (+66 sector score) and this name is not participating, which is itself a statement that investors are treating INTU as a legacy software ex-growth asset rather than an AI beneficiary.","what_market_misses":["The de-rating is discounting an outcome the reported numbers have not yet begun to show: revenue decelerated only 120bps, margins expanded, and FCF grew 41.5%. If the impairment is real it should first appear in billings/net revenue retention, not in the multiple alone.","Intuit owns the system of record for millions of SMB ledgers and consumer tax histories \u2014 agentic AI needs that data substrate, which makes disintermediation an execution question rather than an architectural inevitability. The engine flags the theme itself as under-owned (trend 72 vs pricing 53).","At a 11.7% FCF yield and 0.5x net leverage, the buyback is unusually accretive: sustaining the current $5.4B pace retires ~7% of the float annually, so flat EBIT alone compounds per-share value at high-single digits.","Reported FCF margin of 40.4% is inflated by $2.06B of SBC and by 1.9x FCF/net income conversion; the sustainable cash yield is materially lower than the screen suggests \u2014 a point that cuts against the bull case, not for it.","The dataset itself is incomplete (coverage 0.75; no estimate revisions, no guidance feed), so the 30-point expectations gap partly measures what the engine cannot see rather than what the market has got wrong."],"catalysts":["Next quarterly report (~90 days after the 2026-09-09 filing): billings, QuickBooks Online subscriber adds and consumer tax unit share are the variables that either confirm or refute the structural bear case.","Evidence of agent monetization \u2014 pricing uplift or attach rates on AI-assisted tiers \u2014 converting the AI narrative from threat to revenue line.","Aggressive capital return: with 0.5x net leverage and an 11.7% FCF yield, a levered or accelerated repurchase would be a direct statement that management disagrees with the market's terminal-value math.","Continued Technology sector rotation (+66) eventually broadening from AI infrastructure into de-rated application software.","Insider buying or a large institutional position disclosure at these levels (feed not yet connected)."],"risks":["AI agents and free/direct-file alternatives compress consumer tax pricing and volume \u2014 the scenario the -60% drawdown is pricing; if correct, 16x earnings is not cheap because the earnings are the problem.","Deceleration is already underway (15.1%\u219213.9%); a break below ~10% growth would validate the multiple rather than contradict it.","FCF quality: 1.9x conversion and SBC at 9.6% of revenue mean the headline 11.7% FCF yield overstates distributable cash.","A one-month -22.5% move with no engine-flagged fundamental risk implies a negative catalyst (guidance, competitive or regulatory) not captured in this dataset \u2014 an information gap, not an absence of risk.","Macro regime is genuinely unresolved (Goldilocks 26.6%, Contraction 25.4%, Stagflation 23.5%); SMB software spend is cyclically exposed to small-business formation and failure rates.","Buybacks executed into a falling knife destroy value if the de-rating reflects real impairment."],"thesis_break_conditions":["TTM revenue growth falls below 9% or quarterly billings growth turns negative.","Operating margin compresses more than 200bps YoY, signalling price-driven defence of share.","QuickBooks Online subscriber growth or consumer tax units decline sequentially on a like-for-like basis.","ROIC falls below 15%.","Price fails to reclaim the 50-day (~325) within two quarters and makes a lower low below $277 on expanding volume.","Free cash flow conversion normalises toward 1.0x, revealing the 40% FCF margin as timing-driven.","AI Software & Agents theme trend drops below 45, or Technology rotation score turns below -20 for two consecutive runs.","Adverse regime (Stagflation + Contraction) probability exceeds 55%."],"second_order_beneficiaries":["Hyperscale cloud and inference providers: whichever way the agent war resolves, Intuit must spend on compute to defend the workflow \u2014 its R&D is already $3.38B and rising cash generation funds it.","Payments and embedded-fintech rails (money movement, payroll funding, lending-as-a-service): as software pricing gets commoditised by AI, monetisation migrates to transaction take-rate, benefiting the processors and BaaS providers underneath.","Identity, fraud and verification vendors: agentic filing and automated bookkeeping raise the authentication and audit-trail burden, creating spend that did not exist in a human-in-the-loop world.","Professional accounting and tax-practice software vendors: if consumers shift from DIY to AI-assisted-plus-professional-review, the pro channel captures displaced volume.","Buyers of de-rated, cash-generative application software \u2014 private equity and strategic acquirers \u2014 for whom an 8.5x P/FCF asset with 0.5x leverage is an LBO-able balance sheet.","Index and quant value funds forced to add a name that has moved from growth to value buckets, a mechanical flow that is separate from the fundamental debate."],"epistemic_labels":[{"statement":"TTM revenue $21.45B, +13.9% YoY; operating margin 27.4% (+129bps); FCF $8.66B, +41.5%; ROIC 20.0%; net debt/EBITDA 0.49x.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"Valuation sits at the 0th percentile of its own 5-year range on P/E, EV/Sales, P/FCF and EV/EBITDA, vs medians of 75x, 12.2x, 38.9x and 53.2x.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"Price is -60.4% over 12 months, -31.6% below the 200-day, RSI 29.9, MACD histogram -6.07.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"Buybacks of $5.4B and dividends of $1.35B produced a 9.1% shareholder yield with diluted shares -2.1% YoY.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"SBC of $2.06B equals 9.6% of revenue and FCF conversion of 1.9x net income means headline FCF overstates sustainable owner earnings.","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"A 4-5x multiple compression against improving margins implies the market is repricing terminal value, not near-term earnings.","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"The de-rating is driven primarily by fear of agentic-AI disintermediation of DIY tax and SMB bookkeeping.","kind":"speculative_hypothesis"},{"statement":"Ownership of the SMB ledger and consumer tax data allows Intuit to monetise agents rather than be replaced by them.","kind":"speculative_hypothesis"},{"statement":"The one-month -22.5% decline reflects a specific negative catalyst not present in this dataset.","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"Technology sector rotation score is +66, the highest of any sector in the dataset, while this stock has not participated.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"The engine's own break condition 'price closes >10% below its 200-day average' is already triggered at -31.6%.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"Estimate-revision and management-guidance feeds are not connected, leaving coverage at 0.75.","kind":"observed_fact"}],"confidence":0.45}},"technical":{"score":0,"passes":0,"criteria":{"above_150_200":false,"150_above_200":false,"200_rising_1m":false,"50_above_150_200":false,"above_50":false,"25pct_above_52w_low":false,"within_25pct_of_52w_high":false,"rs_positive_6m":false},"ready":false,"stage":"basing_or_downtrend","close":277.13,"sma50":325.03,"sma150":351.2,"sma200":405.33,"sma150_prev4w":369.53,"sma150_declining":true,"pct_above_52w_low":8.6,"pct_from_52w_high":-60.3,"rs_6m":-54.9,"rsi14":29.9,"atr20":13.876,"atr_pct":5.01,"overbought":f